  "body": {
    "id": "lem:projection-output-bound",
    "kind": "lemma",
    "statement": "Fix \\((P,B^0,\\varepsilon,\\pi_0)\\in\\mathfrak M_{p,m}^{\\mathrm{pub}}\\) and its observed moments \\(\\mathcal O_G\\). For every \\(A\\subseteq V\\), each retained fragment in \\(H_A\\) is the projection onto rows indexed by \\(A\\) of at least one tuple in \\(\\Theta_G(\\mathcal O_G)\\). Distinct fragments at \\(A\\) project to disjoint nonempty output subsets, and therefore \\(|H_A|\\le N_{\\mathrm{out}}\\), \\(\\sum_{A\\subseteq V}|H_A|\\le2^pN_{\\mathrm{out}}\\), and the number of attempted fragment transitions is at most \\(p2^pN_{\\mathrm{out}}\\).",
    "free_symbols": [
      "P",
      "B0",
      "epsilon",
      "pi0",
      "M_pub",
      "p",
      "m",
      "O_G",
      "G",
      "A",
      "V",
      "H_A",
      "Theta_G",
      "N_out"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "def:published-limvam-class",
      "thm:published-all-orders-covariance-compatible",
      "lem:live-fragment-right-congruence",
      "def:fragment-hashcons-enumerator",
      "def:identified-tuple-set",
      "lem:original-row-invariance",
      "def:live-fragment-completions"
    ],
    "proof_tex": "Let \\(\\mathcal P_A\\) be the set of full-lattice prefixes from \\(\\varnothing\\) to \\(A\\).  Induction on \\(|A|\\), using \\(\\texttt{def:fragment-hashcons-enumerator}\\), gives\n\\[\n H_A=\\{F(\\rho):\\rho\\in\\mathcal P_A\\}.\n \\tag{10}\n\\]\nThe initialization proves (10) for \\(A=\\varnothing\\).  Every nonempty prefix to \\(A'\\) has a final edge \\(A'\\setminus\\{r\\}\\to A'\\); by induction its parent fragment is present, and the transition writes exactly \\(\\beta(A'\\setminus\\{r\\},r)\\).  Conversely, every insertion extends a represented prefix by one full-lattice edge.  Exact trie equality removes precisely duplicate fragments.\n\nFix \\(F\\in H_A\\) and a representing prefix \\(\\rho\\).  Choose any suffix.  The resulting permutation belongs to \\(\\Pi_G(\\mathcal O_G)\\) by \\(\\texttt{thm:published-all-orders-covariance-compatible}\\), so its tuple lies in \\(\\Theta_G(\\mathcal O_G)\\).  By \\(\\texttt{lem:original-row-invariance}\\), every \\(T\\in\\operatorname{Comp}(\\rho)\\) satisfies\n\\[\n T\\big|_{\\text{rows indexed by }A}=F.\n \\tag{11}\n\\]\nThe nonempty completion sets for unequal fragments are disjoint by \\(\\texttt{lem:live-fragment-right-congruence}\\) and are subsets of \\(\\Theta_G(\\mathcal O_G)\\).  Hence\n\\[\n |H_A|\\le|\\Theta_G(\\mathcal O_G)|=N_{\\mathrm{out}}.\n \\tag{12}\n\\]\nSumming (12) over all \\(2^p\\) subsets gives \\(\\sum_A|H_A|\\le2^pN_{\\mathrm{out}}\\).  Since each retained fragment is processed once and each subset has at most \\(p\\) outgoing edges,\n\\[\n \\sum_{A\\subseteq V}(p-|A|)|H_A|\n \\le p\\sum_{A\\subseteq V}|H_A|\n \\le p2^pN_{\\mathrm{out}}.\n\\]",
    "justification": "The full-lattice projection charge bounds intermediate published fragments by published numerical outputs.",
    "gap": "The number of compatible orders can be factorial even when the coefficient image is small.",
    "consumer": "The full-lattice implementation obtains output-sensitive storage and transition bounds.",
